  "text": "MMSU - University | Information Resource Facilities GOV.PH TRANSPARENCY QUALITY ASSURANCE CITIZEN'S CHARTER {{ date }} {{ time }} Mariano\n                                Marcos State University Home University Academic Research Extension Global Affairs News e-Services Downloads Home Colleges Agriculture Food & Sustainable Development Aquatic Science & Applied  Technology Arts and Sciences Business, Economics & Accountancy Computing and Information Sciences Engineering Health Sciences Industrial Technology Teacher Education Medicine Law Dentistry Veterinary Medicine Graduate School Campus Facilities F.E.M Hall Information Resource Facilities Information Technology Center Cafeteria & Auxiliary Buildings Events & Social Facilities Health and Wellness Support Centers Sports Facilities University Centers Research Centers College-Based Centers Parks and Open Spaces F.E.M Park S&T Park Sunken Garden Biodiversity Park Salinged Park Small Water Ponds Special Centers & Facilities Air Ambient Monitoring Station Agro-Industrial Economic Zone Religious Facilities Agro-Meteorology Station Information Resource Facilities The University Library System is composed of the Main Library in the Batac campus and the unit libraries and reading centers in the colleges. The Main Library houses thousands of volumes of learning materials in print, electronic, and other formats. It also has special collections on specific subjects including those on Ilokano culture. It also houses the American Corner and the Chinese Corner. Located at the first floor of the Main Library building is the MMSU Museum while the second floor houses the Center for Flexible Learning. University Library International Corner CFL 2nd Floor Visit Website On this page Mariano Marcos State University Brgy. 16-S Quiling Sur, City of Batac Ilocos Norte, Philippines 2906 op@mmsu.edu.ph (63)(077) 600 1234 Quick Links MMSU Citizen's Charter Privacy Notice Opportunities Downloads Library Document Tracking Publication